          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #InCombinatorialModelCategories.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              there exists functorial factorizations into
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                  followed by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  followed by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
            %p
              hence in particular there exists functoral
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
              and functorial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
          This is due to unpublished results by
          = succeed "," do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
          %a{:href => "#Dugger01"} Dugger (2001), Prop. 2.3 and §7
          and
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Barwick10"} Barwick (2010), Prop. 2.5
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              All
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+systems"} orthogonal factorization systems
              are automatically functorial.
          %p
          .num_remark
