                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod
              respects the points says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_M
              is an identity. Thus,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = f_R \circ f_L
              is a factorization. For functoriality, the functoriality of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              gives the commutative square
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \circ f = f_R \circ E(h,k)
              and the functoriality of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(-,-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_L
              gives the commutative square
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi L
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(h,k) \circ f = f_L \circ h
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorization+system"} algebraic weak factorization system
            is a functorial factorization together with compatible enhancements of these endofunctors to a monad and comonad. This can often be detected with the help of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition+law+for+factorizations"} composition law for factorizations
